WEBVTT

00:04.200 --> 00:06.970
<i>After their battle with Stepping Man,</i>

00:06.970 --> 00:10.420
<i>the Survivors spent a lot of time in bed.</i>

00:11.080 --> 00:13.760
<i>In addition to the physical 
damage they'd taken,</i>

00:13.760 --> 00:16.440
<i>they all had a lot on their minds, I'm sure.</i>

00:17.950 --> 00:21.250
<i>Whenever they don't have something 
to occupy their minds,</i>

00:21.250 --> 00:22.970
<i>humans start to think about things.</i>

00:23.430 --> 00:28.130
<i>They think about the things they'd 
been too busy to think about.</i>

00:28.130 --> 00:30.860
<i>The things they'd tried not to think about.</i>

00:33.640 --> 00:35.330
<i>You can't believe in humanity...</i>

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:37.550 --> 00:42.510
"Adventurers Can't Save the World Yet!"

00:48.520 --> 00:51.020
What city are we heading to next, Dad?

00:52.580 --> 00:54.650
We're heading back to Labyrinth City
for the first time in ages.

00:55.430 --> 00:58.150
You remember Uncle Argas, right?

00:58.150 --> 01:00.250
He gave me a pat on the head!

01:00.250 --> 01:01.620
Do I get to see him again?

01:06.090 --> 01:07.670
What is it, Dad?

01:16.120 --> 01:18.550
Your mom and dad both love you very much.

01:18.860 --> 01:20.300
Mom?

01:23.850 --> 01:26.080
You saved us, Argas!

01:26.880 --> 01:28.980
Wh-Why?

02:19.280 --> 02:20.680
I'm sorry.

02:24.330 --> 02:25.980
The Sticky Aqueducts.

02:25.980 --> 02:29.510
The lowest ranked adventurers 
get their start here.

02:29.920 --> 02:33.070
I'm an adventurer starting 
today, right, Mister Argas?

02:33.070 --> 02:37.500
Yes. And now that you're an 
adventurer, it's just "Argas."

02:37.720 --> 02:41.580
All adventurers are equal. Listen, Nick.

02:41.580 --> 02:45.390
Adventurers have to trust each other!

02:44.740 --> 02:46.530
It's chewing grass!

02:46.530 --> 02:47.770
Is that grass yummy?

02:48.810 --> 02:51.600
Just don't let your guard 
down, or you'll regret it.

02:51.600 --> 02:53.580
I know that, Mister Argas!

02:56.480 --> 02:59.020
That's what I meant by 
letting your guard down.

03:10.720 --> 03:13.840
<i>Part of the reason I became an 
adventurer was to make a living.</i>

03:13.840 --> 03:16.810
<i>But the main reason was that I 
thought that if I had been stronger,</i>

03:16.810 --> 03:20.480
<i>I could've helped fight 
alongside Mom and Dad.</i>

03:23.600 --> 03:27.440
<i>When I joined Masters of War, 
Argas gave me a short sword.</i>

03:36.240 --> 03:39.050
<i>What made me happier than 
anything was that he chose it</i>

03:39.050 --> 03:40.750
<i>because he thought it would help me learn.</i>

03:44.180 --> 03:46.340
<i>That's all in the past now.</i>

03:46.340 --> 03:50.180
<i>I've absorbed the past
and made it a part of me.</i>

03:51.210 --> 03:54.730
<i>But, sometimes, I look back with regrets.</i>

03:55.590 --> 03:59.690
<i>If I'd done something different that 
one time, or that other time...</i>

04:00.460 --> 04:06.180
<i>If I'd given Argas a different answer, 
would I still be part of Masters of War?</i>

04:07.540 --> 04:13.460
<i>If I hadn't run away then, would I have 
been able to die alongside my parents?</i>

04:14.540 --> 04:16.760
<i>If I'd...</i>

04:44.960 --> 04:46.120
Agate?

04:51.520 --> 04:53.570
What's Agate doing here?

04:55.490 --> 04:58.580
And what does it mean for me that I can tell 
it's her just by seeing the back of her head?

04:59.780 --> 05:03.830
This isn't good... It looks 
like it'll rain for a while.

05:03.830 --> 05:05.580
Good timing.

05:05.580 --> 05:07.900
I was wondering how I'd 
give this back to you.

05:08.660 --> 05:11.900
This is my...

05:17.140 --> 05:20.650
Which means you're, um...

05:21.150 --> 05:24.380
You know, I never got your name.

05:24.380 --> 05:25.420
I'm...

05:26.660 --> 05:28.860
just a stray dog who loves idols.

05:29.620 --> 05:31.060
You are?

05:31.600 --> 05:35.430
Then... I'm Agate, and I'm just an idol.

05:37.340 --> 05:39.450
It was raining that day, too, wasn't it?

05:39.790 --> 05:40.530
Yeah...

05:41.030 --> 05:45.300
You were out there in the 
rain without an umbrella,

05:45.300 --> 05:48.180
so I couldn't help but talk to you.

05:48.180 --> 05:51.510
I'm glad to find out you have a house!

05:52.350 --> 05:55.960
Oh, you know, a girl from my agency...

05:54.550 --> 05:58.970
Sorry, are you going to keep 
talking like this for a while?

05:59.500 --> 06:01.510
Is it a bother?

06:01.510 --> 06:04.710
No, it's not a bother, but...

06:04.710 --> 06:06.870
Then let me talk a little more.

06:07.410 --> 06:08.570
Okay.

06:11.610 --> 06:16.440
Maybe that day was what saved me.

06:16.440 --> 06:18.350
Did you say something?

06:18.350 --> 06:19.590
No.

06:19.590 --> 06:24.400
Mr. Stray Dog, do you sometimes hear things?

06:24.730 --> 06:25.700
Quiet.

06:32.060 --> 06:32.930
Hey.

06:34.450 --> 06:35.410
Am I still holding onto this?

06:37.000 --> 06:38.660
Until the rain stops.

06:55.420 --> 06:56.610
That'll do.

07:00.290 --> 07:03.720
Are you the one who killed Nalgava?

07:07.070 --> 07:08.040
Yes.

07:09.080 --> 07:10.260
That was me.

07:10.670 --> 07:12.060
I knew it!

07:12.060 --> 07:13.430
Which means I win!

07:13.430 --> 07:17.630
I knew it! You killed him so 
you could take his place!

07:18.240 --> 07:20.230
Ow...

07:20.230 --> 07:23.310
You don't need to be making bets 
after breaking three ribs.

07:23.710 --> 07:25.540
You don't get it, Doc.

07:25.800 --> 07:29.180
If I'd lost, I was gonna lose another three!

07:29.690 --> 07:31.750
Since you won, does that mean 
you get to grow three more?

07:36.280 --> 07:38.610
That's impossible, duh.

07:38.610 --> 07:40.800
Man, I'm a little worried about our new doc!

07:44.510 --> 07:45.800
<i>Medicine's a wonderful thing.</i>

07:46.660 --> 07:50.000
<i>You can help others, even if only a little.</i>

07:50.000 --> 07:53.710
<i>And while you're helping, you don't 
have to think about things.</i>

07:54.790 --> 07:59.530
<i>Strangely, even after all
the terrible things he did,</i>

08:00.290 --> 08:04.730
<i>I can't bring myself to hate 
Stepping Man... Nalgava.</i>

08:05.960 --> 08:12.250
<i>Maybe I took his place as a way to mourn 
him, or maybe I'm just doing it for myself.</i>

08:13.470 --> 08:16.410
<i>Maybe they're the same thing, actually.</i>

08:16.980 --> 08:18.250
<i>I just...</i>

08:18.700 --> 08:20.080
Doctor...

08:22.020 --> 08:23.750
Thanks.

08:31.100 --> 08:31.900
Of course.

08:39.560 --> 08:43.440
<i>I keep waking up, again and again.</i>

08:56.560 --> 09:01.080
<i>Once again, the promise of some 
small salvation makes me suffer...</i>

09:02.080 --> 09:03.470
<i>But is that really true?</i>

09:04.070 --> 09:08.040
<i>Is life that cruel?</i>

09:08.620 --> 09:13.560
<i>Is there really no salvation 
in going forward every day,</i>

09:14.040 --> 09:16.250
<i>even if each day's progress 
is too small to see?</i>

09:21.160 --> 09:24.410
<b>Hono Draco
Rases Horn
Dragon King</b>

09:21.900 --> 09:26.320
<i>Gambling's not supposed to be something 
you do unless you feel like you'll win.</i>

09:26.750 --> 09:30.550
<i>But even if I don't feel like coming, 
I still want my daily life back.</i>

09:30.550 --> 09:32.500
<i>So I'm spending my days imitating 
the life I had before.</i>

09:33.920 --> 09:36.190
<i>I'm a lucky girl, to be able to do that.</i>

09:37.480 --> 09:39.110
<i>I've got no problems with life right now.</i>

09:39.630 --> 09:46.020
<i>Right now, nobody's lying 
to me or trying to get me.</i>

09:46.020 --> 09:47.640
<i>Things are going well.</i>

09:48.250 --> 09:50.120
<i>How could I have a problem with this?</i>

09:50.120 --> 09:51.070
Oh...

09:53.250 --> 09:54.500
I won.

09:55.410 --> 09:58.190
<i>I keep winning and losing. 
I haven't made or lost money.</i>

10:00.150 --> 10:01.130
<i>But...</i>

10:02.250 --> 10:03.440
<i>I'm bored.</i>

10:10.260 --> 10:11.420
It's good.

10:12.140 --> 10:14.450
<i>I wonder if Curran would eat this.</i>

10:19.340 --> 10:20.840
Morning!

10:21.070 --> 10:22.750
Morning!

10:22.750 --> 10:24.590
Hey, it's been a while.

10:25.830 --> 10:27.110
Guys...

10:29.160 --> 10:32.090
H-Have you all been doing well?

10:32.090 --> 10:33.500
I guess.

10:39.230 --> 10:41.640
You're still doing it?

10:44.140 --> 10:47.190
We agreed to stay out of each 
other's private lives, right?

10:47.700 --> 10:51.240
O-Oh, that's right.

10:53.810 --> 10:58.200
<i>What happened with the 
Stepping Man incident was sad.</i>

10:58.200 --> 11:00.500
<i>But it ended the way it should have.</i>

11:01.660 --> 11:06.630
<i>We need to accept the life we have now, 
where we're not lacking for anything.</i>

11:08.270 --> 11:12.280
<i>But right now, everyone's a little distant.</i>

11:12.520 --> 11:17.090
<i>Everybody feels like they're struggling 
against something they can't quite figure out.</i>

11:29.600 --> 11:32.700
Survivors Law #1.

11:33.260 --> 11:35.950
No interfering with other people's hobbies.

11:37.010 --> 11:39.300
Nothing you say will make a difference.

11:40.470 --> 11:45.130
If I wanted to, I could 
just take you and...

11:46.270 --> 11:47.880
Very true.

11:49.090 --> 11:52.250
If you want to be a doctor in 
a dangerous place like this...

11:57.120 --> 12:00.720
You'll need my power.

12:01.200 --> 12:03.000
Think of me as your bodyguard.

12:04.710 --> 12:06.180
Thank you.

12:08.420 --> 12:09.690
Morning!

12:10.090 --> 12:11.680
Morning!

12:11.680 --> 12:14.840
That's the latest edition 
of <i>Lemuria Monthly</i>!

12:15.230 --> 12:17.490
Olivia's still at it.

12:17.490 --> 12:18.550
Let's see...

12:18.550 --> 12:22.170
"Top 100 Weirdos of Labyrinth City."

12:22.620 --> 12:24.190
Are you guys all...

12:27.700 --> 12:29.890
Did you guys already eat?

12:31.070 --> 12:33.400
Huh? Yeah...

12:34.080 --> 12:38.430
I opted for the all-night package, 
so I ate a little at Red's place.

12:38.690 --> 12:40.310
I only ever have a smoke for breakfast.

12:41.850 --> 12:43.240
I see.

12:43.240 --> 12:46.080
Then maybe I'll go eat something.

12:55.620 --> 12:59.080
<i>Was everyone already able to forget?</i>

13:00.240 --> 13:01.810
<i>I can't.</i>

13:03.090 --> 13:06.460
<i>Calios... my old party leader...</i>

13:07.280 --> 13:10.790
<i>The one I once swore loyalty to.</i>

13:12.060 --> 13:17.300
<i>I was deceived by him, abandoned... 
He stole everything I had.</i>

13:18.420 --> 13:23.680
<i>Even if they lied to me, my days 
adventuring with White Heron were fun.</i>

13:24.380 --> 13:26.900
<i>But... I'll never forgive Calios,</i>

13:26.900 --> 13:30.730
<i>the man who stole the Dragon King's 
Jewel, the pride of my clan.</i>

13:30.730 --> 13:33.120
<i>There hasn't been a single day
where I've forgotten him.</i>

13:33.670 --> 13:37.380
You're a Tigerian! You need to be careful!

13:37.380 --> 13:40.580
I didn't do anything, though!

13:40.580 --> 13:45.210
It's okay to be careless, occasionally.
But it's not nice to lie.

13:45.210 --> 13:47.660
But I really didn't...

13:47.660 --> 13:50.520
"You look like you just came out 
of the backwoods,

13:51.550 --> 13:54.690
but here in the Labyrinth City, 
we take these things seriously.

13:56.420 --> 14:00.200
You can buy it for half price, 
or would you rather..."

14:00.200 --> 14:02.150
Y-You...

14:02.420 --> 14:05.280
Want to see what happens if 
she scratches that pendant?

14:13.000 --> 14:13.960
Curran.

14:17.700 --> 14:20.370
Huh? What are you guys up to?

14:20.370 --> 14:23.030
We heard they're preparing 
for the Summersleep Festival.

14:23.030 --> 14:24.810
So we're off to take a look.

14:25.240 --> 14:26.800
Summersleep Festival?

14:27.220 --> 14:30.090
That's right, the Summersleep Festival.

14:30.090 --> 14:34.660
They say that around this time of year, 
the monsters all become calm.

14:36.680 --> 14:38.760
Will there be good food?

14:38.760 --> 14:40.430
I'd guess so, yeah.

14:41.190 --> 14:42.180
I can't wait!

14:43.720 --> 14:48.480
<i>Will the rage that was once 
so strong fade away some day?</i>

14:48.880 --> 14:52.110
<i>If it does, is that a good 
thing or a bad thing?</i>

14:52.540 --> 14:53.840
<i>I couldn't tell you.</i>

14:54.110 --> 14:58.210
<i>The more you care about the present, 
the further away the past gets.</i>

14:59.060 --> 15:03.040
<i>Maybe you're just supposed to care 
about the things that remain?</i>

15:03.840 --> 15:08.070
<i>If that's true, then I only want 
the things I love to remain.</i>

15:11.870 --> 15:14.890
<i>Dragonians are a proud race, with a destiny.</i>

15:15.220 --> 15:19.590
<i>Their destiny is to serve the human who 
will become the hero, and save the world.</i>

15:20.660 --> 15:25.030
<i>I'm a Dragonian. The daughter 
of the Tsubaki Clan leader.</i>

15:25.030 --> 15:26.470
<i>Curran Tsubaki!</i>

15:27.400 --> 15:31.350
<i>A proud Dragoon, protected by 
the grace of the Fire Dragon!</i>

15:32.810 --> 15:34.700
Big news!

15:34.700 --> 15:37.360
Big news! Big news!

15:38.870 --> 15:40.150
Olivia?

15:40.150 --> 15:44.010
Extra! Extra! Read all about it!

15:44.010 --> 15:47.980
A special, extra issue of <i>Lemuria Monthly</i>!

15:47.980 --> 15:49.550
What's this about, Olivia?

15:49.550 --> 15:53.390
Big news, everyone. Extremely big news.

15:53.390 --> 15:54.930
Seems big, yeah.

15:54.930 --> 15:56.220
It certainly is!

15:56.730 --> 15:58.760
What's going on?

15:58.760 --> 16:01.030
This is no time to stay calm!

16:01.030 --> 16:03.900
Get excited or I won't tell you.

16:03.900 --> 16:05.260
Wh-Wh-What?!

16:05.260 --> 16:07.910
Whatever in the world is happening?

16:07.910 --> 16:09.870
Great, that's perfect.

16:09.870 --> 16:12.940
I don't like people who try to 
manipulate others' emotions.

16:12.940 --> 16:16.480
A shocking story is breaking 
even as we speak!

16:16.480 --> 16:22.220
What's this? "Legendary Dark Demon 
God on the Verge of Reviving"?

16:22.470 --> 16:23.940
"...Say Rumors"?

16:23.940 --> 16:26.590
Hey, don't steal my big reveal!

16:26.590 --> 16:29.010
You're the one who was 
flinging papers everywhere.

16:29.010 --> 16:30.590
More fake news?

16:31.000 --> 16:35.840
If you keep spreading lies, 
eventually nobody's going to believe you.

16:35.840 --> 16:40.270
But, this time, I've got verified sources.

16:40.270 --> 16:42.230
What? Really?

16:42.230 --> 16:44.710
I can see Kizuna's smart enough 
to know what this means.

16:44.710 --> 16:45.850
Right!

16:45.850 --> 16:47.350
It means she's making stuff up.

16:49.330 --> 16:51.870
What if I said White Mask was involved?

16:51.870 --> 16:53.160
Really?

16:53.160 --> 16:55.500
I don't know for sure yet...

16:57.210 --> 16:59.750
But what if I said I'd 
located the black market

16:59.750 --> 17:02.200
that was dealing in Illusion King's Jewels?

17:02.620 --> 17:03.850
You did?

17:03.850 --> 17:05.000
Not yet.

17:06.560 --> 17:07.830
Ahem!

17:07.830 --> 17:11.410
I haven't found it yet, but my job's 
to take things that seem suspicious

17:11.410 --> 17:14.360
and combine them into a 
sensational news article.

17:14.360 --> 17:16.750
It's not news if you make it up.

17:16.750 --> 17:18.010
Of course!

17:18.010 --> 17:20.120
Where there's smoke, there's fire!

17:20.120 --> 17:23.000
And if there's no fire, it's a 
gossip rag's job to start one!

17:23.700 --> 17:27.050
You realize you're saying 
you're a fraud, right?

17:27.050 --> 17:30.940
A fraud? No. A romanticist!

17:30.940 --> 17:32.110
A romanticist!

17:32.110 --> 17:33.540
A romanticist, Kizuna!

17:33.540 --> 17:36.320
A romanticist! How exciting!

17:36.320 --> 17:38.030
Would they deal...

17:39.350 --> 17:41.940
in a Dragon King's Jewel, too?

17:41.940 --> 17:43.050
Curran...

17:44.850 --> 17:50.150
To be honest, I don't think I 
should be obsessing over Calios.

17:50.740 --> 17:54.760
But I don't know what I should do!

17:55.190 --> 18:00.840
I'm having fun with all of you, but it 
feels like there's something I'm avoiding!

18:03.250 --> 18:04.460
Why not go for it?

18:06.120 --> 18:09.680
If you can't get over it, 
then go chasing after it.

18:10.240 --> 18:14.510
But, this time, you're not alone.

18:14.510 --> 18:15.460
Yes.

18:15.460 --> 18:19.570
Just make it a job, 
like we did with Stepping Man.

18:21.390 --> 18:22.630
Nick...

18:23.880 --> 18:25.500
It's fine by me.

18:25.500 --> 18:31.130
We're the Survivors. We'll come 
back alive, no matter who we face.

18:31.770 --> 18:34.580
A connection between 
Nalgava and White Mask...

18:34.580 --> 18:37.340
We knew there had to be one.

18:37.580 --> 18:41.120
And we can guess at other connections... 
I've heard lots of rumors.

18:41.640 --> 18:44.570
Would a bad guy be connected to a good guy?

18:44.570 --> 18:47.090
No, he'd be connected to 
an even bigger bad guy.

18:47.340 --> 18:49.560
And if you keep following 
the chain of bad guys...

18:49.560 --> 18:52.470
eventually you'll find the biggest bad 
guy, and you can teach him a lesson!

18:52.470 --> 18:54.800
That sounds fun.

18:54.800 --> 18:56.500
<i>I think she just manipulated him.</i>

18:56.500 --> 18:58.370
Let's give it a go!

18:58.370 --> 19:00.510
We can go catch <i>all</i> the bad guys!

19:00.510 --> 19:00.940
Huh?

19:00.940 --> 19:02.990
Nick, I want to do it too!

19:02.990 --> 19:04.220
Then we're all in agreement!

19:04.220 --> 19:07.040
Let's all go defeat the legendary 
dark Demon God! Hip, hip, hooray!

19:07.040 --> 19:08.590
Hooray!

19:09.160 --> 19:10.720
Well, sure. I guess.

19:26.810 --> 19:32.520
<b><i>Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World</i></b>

19:26.810 --> 19:32.520
<b><i>Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't 
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World</i></b>

22:07.530 --> 22:10.150
I have a question for you.

22:10.150 --> 22:11.520
Anything.

22:12.160 --> 22:18.260
We artifacts will probably outlive them.

22:18.880 --> 22:24.300
From your perspective, as the "Sword of War" 
that trains mankind and helps them grow,

22:24.300 --> 22:27.520
what do you think of the Survivors?

22:28.800 --> 22:30.910
They're all right, I suppose.

22:30.910 --> 22:33.050
I'd expect a little more ambition

22:33.050 --> 22:36.170
from the people who are going 
to slay the Demon God, though.

22:36.170 --> 22:40.420
Oh? I thought you'd be harder on them.

22:40.670 --> 22:43.010
That wouldn't be fair, would it?

22:43.010 --> 22:47.360
They've only been around for 20 
or so years of their short lives.

22:47.360 --> 22:49.610
I'm amazed they've survived this long.

22:49.610 --> 22:51.040
Clap, clap, clap.

22:51.040 --> 22:54.370
Well, they do call themselves the Survivors.

22:54.790 --> 22:59.070
And a bit of skepticism can 
save you a lot of trouble.

22:59.430 --> 23:01.990
It's their greatest weapon.

23:01.990 --> 23:05.210
And it's something you lose as you grow up.

23:05.580 --> 23:08.200
Or it gets worse, and makes you stubborn.

23:08.200 --> 23:11.190
That's fine. A hard head's a weapon, too.

23:11.190 --> 23:12.370
Agreed.

23:12.370 --> 23:14.820
Let them take their time.

23:14.820 --> 23:18.830
And maybe they will be able to 
defeat the Demon God in the end.

23:21.520 --> 23:23.890
Maybe they will...

23:24.680 --> 23:29.180
<i>Right now, these adventurers 
can't save the world.</i>

